.TH CATALOGUPDATE 1 "2026" "Gershwin Desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
catalogupdate \- update the GNUstep application catalog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B catalogupdate
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ CATALOG_FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B catalogupdate
is a Python script that helps maintain
.I Build/Resources/Catalog.plist
\(em the list of GNUstep applications available in the Gershwin PackageManager.
It can search GitHub for new GNUstep applications, add individual entries,
list existing entries, and check whether catalogued repositories still exist.
.PP
If
.I CATALOG_FILE
is omitted the script searches for
.I Catalog.plist
in
.I ../Build/Resources/
relative to the script\(aqs own location, then in
.I Build/Resources/
relative to the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-list
List all entries currently in the catalog (name and URL), sorted
alphabetically.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-search
Search GitHub for GNUstep Objective-C repositories not yet catalogued.
Runs several built-in search queries and presents the candidates.
Unless
.B \-\-dry\-run
is given the user is asked whether to add all found entries.
.TP
.BI \-q " QUERY"
Append an extra GitHub search query string that is used in addition
to the built-in queries when
.B \-\-search
is active.
.TP
.BI \-a " URL NAME DESCRIPTION"
Add a single entry with the given GitHub
.I URL
(e.g.,
.IR https://github.com/owner/repo ),
display
.IR NAME ,
and
.IR DESCRIPTION .
The entry is silently skipped when the URL is already catalogued.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-check
Check every catalogued repository against the GitHub API and report
any that no longer exist (HTTP\~404).
Exits with status\~1 if any missing repository is found.
.TP
.BI \-t " TOKEN"
GitHub personal access token.
Increases the API rate limit from 60 to 5000 requests/hour.
The environment variable
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
is used if this option is not supplied.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be written without actually modifying the catalog file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or no missing repositories when
.B \-\-check
is used).
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred, or at least one repository was found missing
during
.BR \-\-check .
.SH EXAMPLES
List all currently catalogued applications:
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate --list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search GitHub for new apps and optionally add them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate --search
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search with an additional query:
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate --search -q "user:myorg gnustep"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a single new application:
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate -a https://github.com/owner/MyApp.app MyApp "My new app"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check all entries are still live (useful in CI):
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate --check
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview what a search would add without writing anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
catalogupdate --search --dry-run
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
GitHub personal access token.  See
.BI \-t " TOKEN"
above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Build/Resources/Catalog.plist
The catalog file maintained by this tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plistupdate (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Gershwin Project Contributors.
